/-! ## Section 3: internal LA theorem (Priority B — SUBSTANTIVE)

The single SUBSTANTIVE theorem of R417: under the rank equation
`rank 0 = 1`, the carrier `Fin (rank 0) → ℚ` is ℚ-linearly equivalent
to `ℚ`. This is purely internal linear algebra on `Fin 1 → ℚ`, with
no geometric content. The proof uses `LinearEquiv.funUnique` from
`Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Pi` after `subst`ing the rank equation to
collapse `Fin (rank 0)` to `Fin 1`. -/

/-- **R417 substantive internal LA**: given `rank 0 = 1`, the
degreewise-rank carrier `Fin (rank 0) → ℚ` at degree 0 is ℚ-linearly
equivalent to `ℚ`. KERNEL-PURE; uses `LinearEquiv.funUnique (Fin 1)
ℚ ℚ` from Mathlib. This is the Lean-side LA companion to the paper
claim `dim_ℚ H^0(X, ℚ) = 1`; the paper claim itself remains OPEN. -/
theorem DegreewiseRank_rank0_one_profile_closes
    (rank : ℕ → ℕ) (h0 : rank 0 = 1) :
    Nonempty (DegreewiseRankE7_H rank 0 ≃ₗ[ℚ] ℚ) := by
  -- `DegreewiseRankE7_H rank 0` unfolds to `Fin (rank 0) → ℚ`.
  -- After substituting `rank 0 = 1`, this becomes `Fin 1 → ℚ ≃ₗ[ℚ] ℚ`,
  -- which is `LinearEquiv.funUnique (Fin 1) ℚ ℚ` (since `Fin 1` has
  -- `Unique` instance).
  refine ⟨?_⟩
  show (Fin (rank 0) → ℚ) ≃ₗ[ℚ] ℚ
  rw [h0]
  exact LinearEquiv.funUnique (Fin 1) ℚ ℚ

